# Line endings are part of this repository's data, not a checkout preference.
#
# Source and docs are stored with LF and handed out with LF everywhere, so a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true does not rewrite them under us.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The bundled MIBs are the publisher's bytes, pinned: scripts/update_bundled_mibs.py
# --check compares them to the source byte for byte, and the patches in
# scripts/mib-patches/ are cut against those exact lines. Some publishers ship
# CRLF (IEEE 802.1, a pair of IANA modules) and some LF, so neither conversion
# is right for the set -- git must not touch either of them in either
# direction. See pysnmp/pysmi#171.
pysmi/mibs/asn1/** -text
scripts/mib-patches/*.patch -text

# Test fixtures are compared byte for byte for the same reason.
tests/data/** -text

# Content git has no business inspecting for line endings at all.
*.ico binary
